1
00:00:01,793 --> 00:00:05,088
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:13,096 --> 00:00:14,764
[laughs]

3
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:35,660
-[Natalie] <i>Hello, Lover.</i>
-[Jepoy] <i>Where are my weapons?</i>

4
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:39,164
<i>If you want it, come and get it!</i>

5
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:40,498
[laughs]

6
00:00:40,582 --> 00:00:41,833
<i>Mama, everything is ready.</i>

7
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:43,334
<i>The buyer wants to meet me personally.</i>

8
00:00:43,418 --> 00:00:45,837
<i>So, why don't you just stay here</i>
<i>and hold the fort while I'm gone?</i>

9
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:48,673
<i>It's a wiretapping device.</i>
<i>That way, we can record</i>

10
00:00:48,757 --> 00:00:50,049
<i>and listen in on Red Dragon's transaction.</i>

11
00:00:50,133 --> 00:00:51,926
[Lily] <i>If something doesn't go as planned,</i>

12
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,344
<i>we'll be there right away.</i>

13
00:00:53,428 --> 00:00:55,472
[Helena] <i>Emilia will</i>
<i>eventually lead our group,</i>

14
00:00:55,555 --> 00:00:56,931
<i>so I want you to respect her.</i>

15
00:00:57,015 --> 00:01:00,685
[Diego] <i>We can't afford to fail, Lily.</i>
<i>We have to catch Red Dragon in the act.</i>

16
00:01:00,769 --> 00:01:01,895
<i>Police! Don't move!</i>

17
00:01:01,978 --> 00:01:03,813
[gunfire]

18
00:01:03,897 --> 00:01:05,648
<i>Let's move! What are you waiting for?</i>

19
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:07,650
[Lily]<i> Got you.</i>

20
00:01:08,943 --> 00:01:10,987
<i>Anna? It's not what you think, Anna.</i>

21
00:01:11,946 --> 00:01:15,158
[Lily]<i> I know we're in the middle</i>
<i>of a war, Diego.</i>

22
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,285
<i>But I think it's worth the fight</i>

23
00:01:17,368 --> 00:01:18,828
<i>when you aren't alone.</i>

24
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,539
<i>From now on, let's make it official.</i>

25
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:22,791
<i>Will you be mine?</i>

26
00:01:22,874 --> 00:01:24,209
[Diego] <i>I'm all yours.</i>

27
00:01:24,292 --> 00:01:26,544
<i>The problem is, Mama,</i>
<i>you're left with nothing.</i>

28
00:01:26,628 --> 00:01:27,879
<i>Your account is frozen.</i>

29
00:01:27,962 --> 00:01:30,215
<i>Your properties and assets are gone.</i>

30
00:01:30,298 --> 00:01:32,884
<i>That's where you're wrong, Emilia.</i>

31
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:35,303
[Diego]<i> So, if Red Dragon is hiding money,</i>

32
00:01:35,386 --> 00:01:37,013
<i>I know where we can find it.</i>

33
00:01:37,096 --> 00:01:39,933
[Arnaldo] <i>Diego only manages</i>
<i>to score now because</i>

34
00:01:40,016 --> 00:01:40,975
<i>I'm watching from the sidelines.</i>

35
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:42,852
<i>Now that I'm back,</i>

36
00:01:42,936 --> 00:01:44,562
<i>I'll put him in his rightful place.</i>

37
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:46,397
<i>My baby brother.</i>

38
00:01:50,443 --> 00:01:51,486
Arnaldo.

39
00:01:52,153 --> 00:01:53,696
Ah… Diego.

40
00:01:56,741 --> 00:01:57,742
Arnaldo.

41
00:01:58,535 --> 00:02:01,788
You seem to be coming here more often.

42
00:02:02,455 --> 00:02:03,581
Sorry about that, Lily.

43
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:05,917
But I heard about what happened to Diego.

44
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,753
I just want to make sure he's okay.

45
00:02:08,837 --> 00:02:09,921
So, are you okay, Diego?

46
00:02:10,797 --> 00:02:12,423
Were you hurt?

47
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:15,927
Thanks, Arnaldo. But, Lily and I are fine.

48
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:17,554
Besides, what matters

49
00:02:18,429 --> 00:02:19,931
is that Red Dragon's finally behind bars.

50
00:02:20,515 --> 00:02:21,599
That's good to hear.

51
00:02:23,017 --> 00:02:25,145
I know what my grandmother did was wrong.

52
00:02:25,979 --> 00:02:29,023
And, I know my family's done
a lot of horrible things.

53
00:02:30,233 --> 00:02:32,318
I do feel guilty for all that too.

54
00:02:33,361 --> 00:02:36,698
But I guess all I can do now
is pray for them,

55
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:43,163
and hope that truth and justice prevail

56
00:02:43,246 --> 00:02:44,414
in the end.

57
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:50,712
I also hope you two stay safe
while fighting

58
00:02:50,795 --> 00:02:52,338
for what's right.

59
00:02:55,675 --> 00:02:57,468
[tense music plays]

60
00:02:58,303 --> 00:02:59,846
Your hand's bleeding.

61
00:03:00,305 --> 00:03:02,724
Oh, no. It's nothing.

62
00:03:02,807 --> 00:03:04,225
Just a scratch.

63
00:03:04,934 --> 00:03:07,353
-Are you sure?
-Yeah. I'll be fine.

64
00:03:08,730 --> 00:03:10,023
[Arnaldo exhales]

65
00:03:12,108 --> 00:03:14,569
Well, thank you for visiting your brother.

66
00:03:14,652 --> 00:03:16,571
But, we have to go

67
00:03:16,654 --> 00:03:19,240
because we have important errands to run.

68
00:03:22,535 --> 00:03:23,828
-Let's go.
-Wait, Lily.

69
00:03:24,746 --> 00:03:25,914
Uh…

70
00:03:26,497 --> 00:03:27,957
Sorry, I promise this will be quick.

71
00:03:28,041 --> 00:03:29,959
I just wanted to thank you.

72
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:32,712
For taking care of my brother.

73
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:36,507
Take care.

74
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:38,509
Thanks, Arnaldo.

75
00:03:39,510 --> 00:03:40,511
Let's go.

76
00:03:44,098 --> 00:03:47,977
[unsettling music playing]

77
00:03:50,021 --> 00:03:51,648
[car door opens]

78
00:03:54,442 --> 00:03:55,610
[car door closes]

79
00:03:59,489 --> 00:04:00,365
-Take care.
-We'll be going.

80
00:04:00,448 --> 00:04:01,866
-All right.
-Get that treated, okay?

81
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:03,284
Yes, will do.

82
00:04:03,368 --> 00:04:04,619
-Thank you.
-This is nothing.

83
00:04:11,042 --> 00:04:18,049
[unsettling music playing]

84
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:26,808
[clicks tongue]

85
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:53,543
Here, Anna. Drink something.

86
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:56,379
[sniffles, exhales]

87
00:04:58,256 --> 00:05:00,800
I really can't believe
Jepoy did that to you.

88
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:03,219
Just say the word,
and I'll go teach him a lesson.

89
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,014
Forget it, Marlon.

90
00:05:08,099 --> 00:05:10,310
That'll just make things worse.

91
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:17,066
Sorry.

92
00:05:17,150 --> 00:05:19,068
I'm just really mad at him right now.

93
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,112
He really shouldn't have done that to you.

94
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:27,410
[sobbing]

95
00:05:27,493 --> 00:05:31,456
[soft music playing]

96
00:05:41,007 --> 00:05:42,300
It's okay. Just let it all out.

97
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:52,226
[rattling]

98
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:53,311
[Jepoy] Natalie!

99
00:05:54,228 --> 00:05:55,521
Open the door!

100
00:05:56,439 --> 00:05:57,940
Open the damn door!

101
00:06:00,151 --> 00:06:02,737
[panting]

102
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:05,573
Can you calm down, Madrigal?
You're like a raging bull!

103
00:06:05,656 --> 00:06:07,200
[squeals]

104
00:06:08,159 --> 00:06:10,495
Are you ready for round two? Huh?

105
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:12,872
Anna and I already broke up.

106
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:17,001
Are you happy now?!
Was this what you wanted?!

107
00:06:20,046 --> 00:06:24,717
Your romance with that woman
was doomed from the start!

108
00:06:27,970 --> 00:06:29,388
And, in case you've forgotten…

109
00:06:30,681 --> 00:06:33,476
you were mine first.

110
00:06:37,939 --> 00:06:39,899
She just took you away from me.

111
00:06:41,692 --> 00:06:43,361
Or did you forget?

112
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:49,826
You belong to me.

113
00:06:51,410 --> 00:06:52,578
Do you understand?

114
00:06:55,123 --> 00:06:57,583
I trusted Jepoy.

115
00:06:59,585 --> 00:07:01,963
How could he do this to me?

116
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:08,344
Where did I go wrong, Marlon?

117
00:07:09,554 --> 00:07:13,975
Is it because I couldn't give
what Natalie was ready to?

118
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:18,563
Isn't my love enough for him?

119
00:07:23,734 --> 00:07:25,653
Well, I guess it's my fault too.

120
00:07:26,487 --> 00:07:29,365
I fooled myself into thinking
he actually loved me,

121
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:30,700
but he didn't.

122
00:07:33,327 --> 00:07:36,581
Turns out he'd much rather
take care of himself.

123
00:07:40,585 --> 00:07:41,669
Then again…

124
00:07:43,963 --> 00:07:45,923
I guess men are just that selfish.

125
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:49,552
Don't say that.

126
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:52,763
Not all men are like Jepoy.

127
00:08:01,355 --> 00:08:02,648
[squeals]

128
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:03,941
-[grunts]
-[gasps]

129
00:08:04,025 --> 00:08:06,903
[both breathing heavily]

130
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:09,447
-[grunts]
-[shrieks]

131
00:08:20,249 --> 00:08:24,420
[dramatic music playing]

132
00:08:44,774 --> 00:08:46,442
Jepoy's an idiot.

133
00:08:47,485 --> 00:08:50,988
I can't believe he cheated
on a woman like you.

134
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:55,576
You know, Anna…

135
00:08:56,452 --> 00:08:58,829
one day, you'll find a man
who'll treat you right.

136
00:08:59,789 --> 00:09:03,793
The kind who'll never lie, hurt,
or leave you.

137
00:09:06,254 --> 00:09:07,463
Who knows…

138
00:09:08,756 --> 00:09:10,174
he might just be hanging around.

139
00:09:10,967 --> 00:09:12,510
You'll find him, eventually.

140
00:09:14,512 --> 00:09:17,390
One day, I'm sure he'll have
the guts to tell you…

141
00:09:19,684 --> 00:09:20,851
just how he feels.

142
00:09:22,019 --> 00:09:24,230
And then, I'm sure
he'll be ready to make you feel

143
00:09:25,064 --> 00:09:26,649
what true love is like.

144
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:29,485
The kind of love that you deserve.

145
00:09:30,194 --> 00:09:34,031
[piano music playing]

146
00:09:59,390 --> 00:10:00,600
I've got to go.

147
00:10:13,988 --> 00:10:17,325
[tense music playing]

148
00:10:29,211 --> 00:10:30,880
We'll pretend to buy some drinks.

149
00:10:35,968 --> 00:10:37,053
Ma'am?

150
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:44,977
How much for the juice?

151
00:10:47,730 --> 00:10:48,939
Do you want some juice?

152
00:10:49,023 --> 00:10:51,067
Sure. What else do they have?

153
00:10:53,027 --> 00:10:54,904
All right. We'll have two, please.

154
00:10:55,529 --> 00:10:56,572
[Diego whispers] What?

155
00:10:59,283 --> 00:11:01,243
Just wait. I'll go first.

156
00:11:01,327 --> 00:11:02,244
Okay.

157
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:14,256
Here you go.

158
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,515
Looks like it'll be hard to get in.

159
00:11:23,015 --> 00:11:24,809
This place is heavily guarded.

160
00:11:25,351 --> 00:11:27,561
We'll need help from the cops.

161
00:11:28,354 --> 00:11:29,188
No.

162
00:11:30,064 --> 00:11:31,357
Not yet, Diego.

163
00:11:32,608 --> 00:11:34,402
For now, I don't want anyone else
to know about this.

164
00:11:34,485 --> 00:11:36,195
First, we have to make sure

165
00:11:36,278 --> 00:11:39,323
that Red Dragon's money
really is in there.

166
00:11:40,241 --> 00:11:44,120
Don't forget, she has way
too many connections.

167
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:47,623
I don't want her ruining any of our plans.

168
00:11:47,706 --> 00:11:51,460
[upbeat music playing]

169
00:12:12,648 --> 00:12:15,693
Boys, go in. Break time.

170
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:18,654
Wait, don't start the car.

171
00:12:18,737 --> 00:12:21,615
[tense music playing]

172
00:12:31,750 --> 00:12:33,294
[chuckling]

173
00:12:33,377 --> 00:12:35,045
You should have seen their faces.

174
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:37,882
They believed the good Arnaldo act.

175
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:39,216
I don't know why.

176
00:12:39,300 --> 00:12:44,263
Well, I would dare say
that it's really good, my son.

177
00:12:44,346 --> 00:12:45,347
You know…

178
00:12:45,890 --> 00:12:50,686
just continue spying on Lily and Diego.

179
00:12:51,937 --> 00:12:55,357
Because we should always be one step ahead

180
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,026
of all their plans.

181
00:12:58,652 --> 00:13:00,362
Noted, Grandpa. I'll do that.

182
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:03,699
Well, speaking of,

183
00:13:03,782 --> 00:13:06,368
when I got there,
they were in a hurry to leave.

184
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:10,623
They said they needed
to be somewhere important.

185
00:13:11,957 --> 00:13:15,920
Voices inside my head keep telling me…

186
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,339
it has something to do with Grandma.

187
00:13:19,548 --> 00:13:22,301
They're going to do something
to keep Grandma in prison.

188
00:13:24,011 --> 00:13:26,096
Well, just like what I told you.

189
00:13:26,847 --> 00:13:30,851
We need to know
what those two are planning.

190
00:13:32,228 --> 00:13:37,107
We need to weaken them from the inside.

191
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:39,818
And with you…

192
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:44,073
[chuckling] the good Arnaldo being there…

193
00:13:44,782 --> 00:13:47,409
they will never know what hit them.

194
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:49,870
Well…

195
00:13:52,122 --> 00:13:55,543
to the fall of Lily and Diego

196
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:58,796
and the rise of the Ardientes.

197
00:13:59,463 --> 00:14:01,298
I'll drink to that.

198
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,550
[glasses clink]

199
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:16,939
[tense music playing]

200
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,440
Twenty minutes.

201
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:23,445
They have a twenty-minute break.

202
00:14:26,490 --> 00:14:31,704
That's the amount of time
we have to scale the wall.

203
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:39,295
Let's go.

204
00:14:49,138 --> 00:14:50,806
[car engine starts]

205
00:15:04,945 --> 00:15:08,949
Give this to Magbanua.
He knows what to do with that.

206
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:13,412
Emilia!

207
00:15:13,495 --> 00:15:15,205
Oh, please join me!

208
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:18,709
What's happening to your mother?

209
00:15:18,792 --> 00:15:22,880
It seems like she doesn't
want to leave prison.

210
00:15:23,297 --> 00:15:24,798
Does she like it in there?

211
00:15:25,466 --> 00:15:28,510
Ask her when
the housewarming party will be

212
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:31,096
so that we can visit her.

213
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:34,433
Go ahead, Papa. Laugh all you want.

214
00:15:34,516 --> 00:15:36,936
But you know, this is all temporary, Papa.

215
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:39,855
When we both get back on our feet,

216
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,398
we'll forget you even exist.

217
00:15:41,482 --> 00:15:42,942
[laughs]

218
00:15:43,025 --> 00:15:45,110
You'll forget I exist?

219
00:15:45,194 --> 00:15:46,278
Hey!

220
00:15:46,362 --> 00:15:48,948
Even if you and your mother join forces,

221
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:52,201
where would you get power from?

222
00:15:52,826 --> 00:15:56,288
Your mother has fallen far from grace.

223
00:15:57,164 --> 00:16:05,214
All the riches of the much-ballyhooed
Red Dragon are gone.

224
00:16:05,297 --> 00:16:07,383
That's what you think, Papa.

225
00:16:07,466 --> 00:16:10,135
It ain't over until the fat lady sings.

226
00:16:10,219 --> 00:16:12,137
Or should I say the Red Dragon sings.

227
00:16:12,221 --> 00:16:17,977
Emilia, how can she make
a comeback when she's dirt poor?

228
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:23,899
The authorities seized all her assets.

229
00:16:24,566 --> 00:16:25,859
She has no money left.

230
00:16:25,943 --> 00:16:28,320
Didn't you learn anything from me?

231
00:16:29,446 --> 00:16:32,741
Money makes the world go around.

232
00:16:32,825 --> 00:16:38,872
And I have it in all kinds of currency.

233
00:16:38,956 --> 00:16:42,668
Wow. Clearly, Papa,
you underestimated Mama.

234
00:16:43,043 --> 00:16:46,338
What the police have
is only the tip of the iceberg.

235
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:50,384
You know, Red Dragon
is more than what meets the eye.

236
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:53,303
And one more thing, Papa.

237
00:16:53,387 --> 00:16:57,599
You know, I will inherit
everything Red Dragon owns.

238
00:16:57,683 --> 00:16:59,643
All the things that you see and don't.

239
00:16:59,727 --> 00:17:01,270
[laughs]

240
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:03,147
Who's laughing now, Papa?

241
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:08,652
[tense music playing]

242
00:17:13,824 --> 00:17:16,118
No matter how solid a wall is built,

243
00:17:16,827 --> 00:17:18,454
cracks form eventually.

244
00:17:19,038 --> 00:17:20,706
And that's what I saw earlier.

245
00:17:21,790 --> 00:17:25,753
But Lily, our biggest problem
is the guards.

246
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,796
There are way too many of them.

247
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:30,841
Every corner of that place
is heavily guarded.

248
00:17:31,508 --> 00:17:33,052
We can't get past them.

249
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,262
I know, Diego.

250
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:41,477
Those CCTV cameras
and those walls never rest.

251
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:46,190
But since those guards are only human,

252
00:17:47,232 --> 00:17:48,692
they get tired too.

253
00:17:50,611 --> 00:17:53,739
<i>Boys, go in. Break time.</i>

254
00:17:57,826 --> 00:17:59,661
We just need to wait.

255
00:17:59,995 --> 00:18:02,372
Let's wait for an opening.

256
00:18:02,831 --> 00:18:06,210
Our mission doesn't have
any room for errors.

257
00:18:06,293 --> 00:18:10,422
[tense music building up]

258
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:24,228
It looks like your grandma's
keeping a secret.

259
00:18:25,979 --> 00:18:29,817
Sneaky, sneaky, Red Dragon.

260
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:32,319
But never mind.

261
00:18:33,570 --> 00:18:37,199
I know how she operates.

262
00:18:38,575 --> 00:18:41,036
A crime lord of her caliber

263
00:18:41,120 --> 00:18:44,623
will not allow something like this.

264
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:48,293
She will not allow her entire fortune

265
00:18:48,377 --> 00:18:50,087
to disappear just like that.

266
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:58,345
So, are you saying that Grandma
still has some money hidden?

267
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:04,143
You are absolutely correct.

268
00:19:05,727 --> 00:19:12,067
Of course, we need to get
our share of her fortune.

269
00:19:13,318 --> 00:19:14,862
We're family, right?

270
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:21,034
And an Ardiente will always find a way

271
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:23,328
to get what he wants.

272
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:25,747
[laughs]

273
00:19:41,597 --> 00:19:45,225
[piano music playing]

274
00:19:57,487 --> 00:19:59,615
Sorry. Sorry. Did I scare you?

275
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:14,671
How are Lily and Diego?
Do you have an update?

276
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:17,591
I don't.

277
00:20:18,175 --> 00:20:19,843
Camia, I want to help them.

278
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:29,770
Sure, Damian.

279
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:52,501
[tense music playing]

280
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,756
Come on. Let's take a quick break.

281
00:21:41,925 --> 00:21:44,386
This is it. This is the blind spot.

282
00:21:48,557 --> 00:21:50,267
We only have a few minutes

283
00:21:50,350 --> 00:21:51,977
before the roving guards come back.

284
00:22:07,242 --> 00:22:08,410
Come on.

285
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:18,420
[door opens]

286
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:22,924
[pensive music playing]

287
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:25,635
Are you lost, Julio Ardiente?

288
00:22:27,429 --> 00:22:28,555
No.

289
00:22:29,431 --> 00:22:34,186
I am exactly where I would like to be.

290
00:22:34,895 --> 00:22:36,354
Visiting me in jail?

291
00:22:37,230 --> 00:22:38,774
For what? To laugh at me?

292
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:44,988
My darling, Helena.
I'm not here to laugh at you.

293
00:22:45,947 --> 00:22:49,201
Nor will I try to be a comedian
to make you laugh.

294
00:22:50,160 --> 00:22:51,369
But

295
00:22:52,412 --> 00:22:55,082
you might laugh

296
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:56,958
when you hear what I'm about to tell you.

297
00:22:57,042 --> 00:23:02,631
[tense music playing]

298
00:23:08,637 --> 00:23:12,390
And you might not be able
to contain your excitement

299
00:23:12,474 --> 00:23:14,059
once you hear my offer.

300
00:23:17,521 --> 00:23:22,359
An alliance is formed between two factions

301
00:23:22,442 --> 00:23:24,986
to defeat a common enemy.

302
00:23:25,070 --> 00:23:27,447
Of course, I know you know that.

303
00:23:28,615 --> 00:23:32,244
You and I have a common enemy.

304
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:36,081
Lily Cruz.

305
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:44,297
And I also know that you know
two dragons are better than one.

306
00:23:48,301 --> 00:23:50,637
Are you listening to me so far?

307
00:23:50,720 --> 00:23:51,847
I'm listening.

308
00:23:52,556 --> 00:23:53,723
Okay.

309
00:23:54,683 --> 00:23:58,812
What if I can tell you
that I can offer you

310
00:23:58,895 --> 00:24:01,773
that alliance against Lily Cruz,

311
00:24:02,524 --> 00:24:04,693
and, most importantly,

312
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:11,658
that I can guarantee your freedom?

313
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:22,836
[tense music playing]

314
00:25:00,749 --> 00:25:01,917
A stare.

315
00:25:02,626 --> 00:25:04,294
Is that all I'm going to get from you?

316
00:25:04,961 --> 00:25:09,174
No feisty reaction?
No passionate declaration?

317
00:25:09,257 --> 00:25:11,009
What do you want me to say?!

318
00:25:11,092 --> 00:25:15,013
A big, fat, juicy yes
would be a good start!

319
00:25:15,096 --> 00:25:16,806
You're too impatient!

320
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:22,062
I am not easy and that
is what you liked about me!

321
00:25:26,399 --> 00:25:29,986
I am not courting you. So don't test me!

322
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:32,739
This is a business offer.

323
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:36,534
If you really know how to strategize,

324
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:40,914
and if you're as intelligent
as I think you are,

325
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:45,001
you will not dare refuse my offer!

326
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:47,128
You haven't learned your lesson!

327
00:25:47,921 --> 00:25:52,842
You should never raise
your voice at a dragon

328
00:25:52,926 --> 00:25:54,928
if you don't want to be eaten alive.

329
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:05,397
[tense music playing]

330
00:26:10,819 --> 00:26:12,404
The inside is teeming with guards.

331
00:26:12,487 --> 00:26:14,489
And the money pit is pretty far from here.

332
00:26:17,993 --> 00:26:19,869
I need to see what's inside, Diego.

333
00:26:19,953 --> 00:26:21,329
I have to.

334
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,373
So we can make
all the necessary preparations.

335
00:26:27,752 --> 00:26:29,004
Be careful, okay?

336
00:26:53,570 --> 00:26:55,155
What? He said that?

337
00:26:55,697 --> 00:26:56,865
Yes.

338
00:26:56,948 --> 00:26:58,366
And what did you say?

339
00:26:59,326 --> 00:27:02,829
I reacted like a true-blue dragon should.

340
00:27:03,371 --> 00:27:05,165
[exhales] Good.

341
00:27:05,248 --> 00:27:07,542
Because you shouldn't fall
for Papa's trap, you know.

342
00:27:08,043 --> 00:27:10,170
I have a feeling he needs
something from you,

343
00:27:10,253 --> 00:27:11,796
that's why he's acting like that.

344
00:27:11,880 --> 00:27:13,256
Wait.

345
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,550
What if he already knows
about your hidden wealth?

346
00:27:16,593 --> 00:27:20,388
You know, Emilia,
I was wondering that too.

347
00:27:21,056 --> 00:27:24,100
Aside from Romulo,
who's now rotting in prison,

348
00:27:25,018 --> 00:27:26,436
you, baby girl,

349
00:27:26,519 --> 00:27:29,189
are the only person who knows
about my hidden wealth.

350
00:27:29,731 --> 00:27:31,941
You didn't mention that
to your father, did you?

351
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:36,821
<i>Emilia, how can she make a comeback</i>

352
00:27:36,905 --> 00:27:38,698
<i>when she's dirt poor?</i>

353
00:27:39,407 --> 00:27:43,870
<i>The authorities seized all her assets.</i>

354
00:27:44,329 --> 00:27:47,123
<i>Clearly, Papa, you underestimated Mama.</i>

355
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:50,960
<i>What the police have</i>
<i>is only the tip of the iceberg.</i>

356
00:27:57,759 --> 00:27:58,760
What?!

357
00:27:58,843 --> 00:28:02,097
Hell no, Mama!
I would never say that to Papa!

358
00:28:02,180 --> 00:28:04,057
I know how confidential that is.

359
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:06,351
Me, tell him about your hidden wealth?

360
00:28:06,434 --> 00:28:09,979
No! I didn't tell him.
I swear my life on it.

361
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:11,689
Never mind.

362
00:28:12,023 --> 00:28:14,692
He'll have a hard time
stealing it, anyway.

363
00:28:15,026 --> 00:28:16,319
Because it is being guarded

364
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:18,696
by the fiercest dragon of them all.

365
00:28:35,547 --> 00:28:37,966
Yes, a dragon.

366
00:28:38,800 --> 00:28:41,261
A big, imposing monster.

367
00:28:45,682 --> 00:28:47,058
You think you can beat it?

368
00:28:47,475 --> 00:28:48,768
Outsmart it?

369
00:28:52,105 --> 00:28:54,941
But nothing can escape
its all-seeing eyes.

370
00:28:55,859 --> 00:28:57,026
Galang, Galang.

371
00:28:57,610 --> 00:28:59,028
Could you check the left wing?

372
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:02,157
[Red Dragon] Because the dragon's eyes

373
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:05,785
can see everything, every
day, twenty-four-seven.

374
00:29:08,872 --> 00:29:13,251
It guards my billions' worth
of cash and treasury bonds.

375
00:29:18,965 --> 00:29:21,676
And whoever dares provoke the dragon…

376
00:29:22,635 --> 00:29:25,180
will spontaneously combust.

377
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:37,901
[evil laughter]

378
00:29:37,984 --> 00:29:40,320
[awkward laughter]

379
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:51,498
Boss, the area is clear.
I'm going back to my post.

380
00:29:52,540 --> 00:29:53,666
Okay.

381
00:30:05,804 --> 00:30:06,888
Okay, boys.

382
00:30:07,472 --> 00:30:10,225
Break time's over. Back to your posts now.

383
00:30:15,188 --> 00:30:18,608
[tense music playing]

384
00:30:27,450 --> 00:30:28,535
Let's go.

385
00:30:43,132 --> 00:30:44,342
I'll leave that to you.

386
00:30:45,885 --> 00:30:49,389
[upbeat music playing]

387
00:30:49,472 --> 00:30:52,934
It won't be easy to get
to Helena's hidden wealth.

388
00:30:53,017 --> 00:30:56,271
We have to use force. We need manpower.

389
00:30:57,021 --> 00:30:58,189
Leave it to me.

390
00:31:00,775 --> 00:31:02,151
[cell phone ringing]

391
00:31:04,028 --> 00:31:05,488
Hello, Atty. Fisher?

392
00:31:11,369 --> 00:31:12,412
What?

393
00:31:15,915 --> 00:31:17,083
Come on, let's go home.

394
00:31:28,803 --> 00:31:29,888
Bless you.

395
00:31:35,602 --> 00:31:36,978
Grandma declined your offer?

396
00:31:38,062 --> 00:31:39,022
[scoffs]

397
00:31:39,105 --> 00:31:40,398
Yes.

398
00:31:41,232 --> 00:31:46,863
Because your grandma
is silly, selfish, stubborn…

399
00:31:46,946 --> 00:31:48,406
And stupid.

400
00:31:49,365 --> 00:31:51,492
Sorry, I had to finish your sentence.

401
00:31:51,576 --> 00:31:52,785
But, seriously.

402
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:56,080
You're offering her a lifeline,
and then she refuses.

403
00:31:58,124 --> 00:32:00,251
Maybe she figured out
we're after her money?

404
00:32:00,335 --> 00:32:03,087
But, what's stopping us from stealing it?

405
00:32:04,547 --> 00:32:06,549
Well, you know…

406
00:32:07,383 --> 00:32:10,720
whether or not
your grandma accepts my offer

407
00:32:10,803 --> 00:32:13,640
to form an alliance, it doesn't matter

408
00:32:13,723 --> 00:32:17,226
because I already have the power.

409
00:32:18,144 --> 00:32:22,315
Her money is just going
to be icing on the cake.

410
00:32:23,691 --> 00:32:25,068
Uh…

411
00:32:25,151 --> 00:32:27,278
Okay. Wait, I'm confused.

412
00:32:27,362 --> 00:32:30,949
Earlier, you wanted to steal
from her, and now, you don't.

413
00:32:31,032 --> 00:32:34,744
So, which is it?
Why the sudden change of heart?

414
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:40,083
You know, grandson, sometimes,
you just have to wait,

415
00:32:40,166 --> 00:32:45,129
and let situations take
their natural course.

416
00:32:45,672 --> 00:32:46,756
Anyway…

417
00:32:47,924 --> 00:32:52,470
whatever happens,
I have my eyes on the prize.

418
00:32:53,429 --> 00:33:00,061
And I assure you that
those riches will go to us.

419
00:33:00,937 --> 00:33:03,064
Just us, and not your mom.

420
00:33:04,273 --> 00:33:05,566
Because if not,

421
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:10,238
I'm going to make sure
that no one else gets it.

422
00:33:10,321 --> 00:33:13,741
I'm going to burn all that money into ash.

423
00:33:15,368 --> 00:33:16,369
Don't worry.

424
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:21,624
Okay. Now, let's eat.

425
00:33:30,383 --> 00:33:31,426
Okay.

426
00:33:32,593 --> 00:33:34,804
Bring those here. Thank you.

427
00:33:39,517 --> 00:33:40,852
[clears throat] Emilia?

428
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:46,733
Is it true that your mother's
got tons of cash hidden?

429
00:33:47,650 --> 00:33:49,527
And where did you hear that from?

430
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:51,946
I just know. It's true, isn't it?

431
00:33:52,905 --> 00:33:54,907
Um, I'm sorry to disappoint you,

432
00:33:54,991 --> 00:33:57,493
my dear husband, but, my lips are sealed.

433
00:33:57,577 --> 00:34:00,496
I cannot reveal anything about my mom

434
00:34:00,580 --> 00:34:02,290
because I made a promise to her.

435
00:34:03,124 --> 00:34:08,463
Come on, everyone in the family
knows each other's secrets.

436
00:34:08,546 --> 00:34:10,173
And, so does the town.

437
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:11,966
You're not hiding anything anymore, right?

438
00:34:12,717 --> 00:34:14,927
And what do you mean by that?

439
00:34:15,553 --> 00:34:18,389
That your father wants to help
free your mother, doesn't he?

440
00:34:18,973 --> 00:34:20,183
I doubt it, Raul.

441
00:34:20,266 --> 00:34:24,062
My mother would never ask
for help from Papa.

442
00:34:24,145 --> 00:34:27,065
She'd rather be in jail
than accept anything from him.

443
00:34:27,815 --> 00:34:29,067
Oh, really?

444
00:34:31,402 --> 00:34:34,489
So, who helped your mother
get out of jail?

445
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:36,074
What are you talking about?

446
00:34:36,783 --> 00:34:38,034
[chuckles]

447
00:34:39,535 --> 00:34:42,789
[tense music playing]

448
00:34:42,872 --> 00:34:46,793
<i>Only ten minutes ago,</i>
<i>the authorities made the decision</i>

449
00:34:46,876 --> 00:34:50,296
<i>to dismiss the charges</i>
<i>against Helena Montoya,</i>

450
00:34:50,379 --> 00:34:52,507
<i>who is suspected</i>
<i>to be the syndicate leader,</i>

451
00:34:52,590 --> 00:34:54,050
<i>Red Dragon.</i>

452
00:34:54,801 --> 00:34:57,303
<i>According to the reports,</i>
<i>there is insufficient evidence</i>

453
00:34:57,386 --> 00:35:00,515
<i>to prove that Helena Montoya</i>
<i>is Red Dragon.</i>

454
00:35:01,057 --> 00:35:02,100
[chuckles]

455
00:35:03,601 --> 00:35:04,602
Why do I get the feeling

456
00:35:04,685 --> 00:35:05,937
you had something to do with this?

457
00:35:08,898 --> 00:35:10,024
[chuckles]

458
00:35:13,277 --> 00:35:15,071
[reporter] <i>The entrapment operation</i>

459
00:35:15,154 --> 00:35:17,115
<i>that led to Ms. Montoya's arrest</i>

460
00:35:17,198 --> 00:35:18,866
<i>was said to be a frame-up</i>

461
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:21,536
<i>set up by her business competitors.</i>

462
00:35:21,619 --> 00:35:24,914
<i>Stay tuned to Ardiente News. This is--</i>

463
00:35:28,042 --> 00:35:29,252
[Marlon] Anna!

464
00:35:30,753 --> 00:35:31,796
Anna!

465
00:35:33,422 --> 00:35:35,174
Good thing I caught you.
I was just at the center.

466
00:35:35,258 --> 00:35:39,804
Yeah, I just stopped by to see
my sick student. What's wrong?

467
00:35:39,887 --> 00:35:41,389
Red Dragon's case was dismissed.

468
00:35:42,682 --> 00:35:43,766
What?

469
00:35:45,560 --> 00:35:47,228
But, Lily and Auntie Camia…

470
00:35:47,812 --> 00:35:49,147
-Let's go see them.
-Yeah.

471
00:35:54,277 --> 00:35:56,404
-How dare you!
-Camia.

472
00:35:56,821 --> 00:35:59,866
You shameless liar! You're a liar!

473
00:35:59,949 --> 00:36:02,910
You are Red Dragon!
There's no way you can hide!

474
00:36:02,994 --> 00:36:06,205
-Camia, calm down.
-You don't understand, Damian.

475
00:36:06,622 --> 00:36:08,708
They always just manage
to escape from the law!

476
00:36:08,791 --> 00:36:10,126
-I know.
-They're nothing but liars!

477
00:36:10,209 --> 00:36:11,460
I know.

478
00:36:12,545 --> 00:36:13,713
I understand how you feel.

479
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:23,973
Tell me, Attorney,
that this is not happening.

480
00:36:24,056 --> 00:36:27,518
You said we filed
a strong case against her.

481
00:36:27,602 --> 00:36:30,188
-Yes, it's true.
-So, what happened?

482
00:36:30,271 --> 00:36:32,273
We even had fiscal evidence!

483
00:36:32,982 --> 00:36:35,818
You know how business in Ardiente works.

484
00:36:36,194 --> 00:36:37,862
And, my gut tells me Red Dragon paid--

485
00:36:37,945 --> 00:36:38,863
[Lily] <i>Enough.</i>

486
00:36:38,946 --> 00:36:42,867
What I want to know is,
do we still have a chance?

487
00:36:42,950 --> 00:36:45,203
The case hasn't gone
through a hearing yet.

488
00:36:45,286 --> 00:36:48,247
So, we can file it again
and it won't be double jeopardy.

489
00:36:48,331 --> 00:36:52,627
Okay. I'll file it again.
Go see Myla right now.

490
00:36:53,085 --> 00:36:54,337
I'm already here, Lily.

491
00:37:04,138 --> 00:37:05,181
Myla?

492
00:37:10,770 --> 00:37:11,771
Myla?

493
00:37:15,358 --> 00:37:16,400
Myla?

494
00:37:16,984 --> 00:37:21,405
[suspenseful music playing]

495
00:37:26,118 --> 00:37:29,330
LILY, THANK YOU FOR EVERYTHING.
BUT I'M SORRY. I CAN'T DO IT. MYLA.

496
00:37:32,875 --> 00:37:34,001
[groans]

497
00:37:39,632 --> 00:37:40,925
Lily!

498
00:37:44,553 --> 00:37:46,389
Even Myla is gone.

499
00:37:48,307 --> 00:37:52,228
She was the only one left
who could testify for us

500
00:37:52,311 --> 00:37:53,562
and now she's gone.

501
00:37:54,188 --> 00:37:56,732
How can I file the case again,

502
00:37:56,816 --> 00:37:59,193
if I don't have anyone
who can testify for me?

503
00:38:02,905 --> 00:38:03,948
You do.

504
00:38:06,951 --> 00:38:08,953
I'll testify against Red Dragon.

505
00:38:12,873 --> 00:38:14,792
-Diego.
-Lily.

506
00:38:25,344 --> 00:38:30,558
Their efforts to prove that
I am Red Dragon have failed.

507
00:38:31,017 --> 00:38:33,436
Because the truth finally prevailed

508
00:38:33,519 --> 00:38:35,688
over their baseless accusations.

509
00:38:36,939 --> 00:38:38,733
Today, justice is served.

510
00:38:39,358 --> 00:38:41,068
I am not Red Dragon.

511
00:38:42,778 --> 00:38:47,867
And no one can prove
I am that wicked crime leader.

512
00:38:48,826 --> 00:38:53,122
I am Helena Montoya.
I am a private citizen.

513
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:56,125
A concerned citizen,
who wants to do nothing

514
00:38:56,208 --> 00:39:01,005
but serve and love the town of Ardiente.

515
00:39:03,299 --> 00:39:05,134
Onward, Ardiente!

516
00:39:05,217 --> 00:39:07,595
[applause]

517
00:39:25,279 --> 00:39:28,949
<i>Go ahead. Smile and celebrate.</i>

518
00:39:29,617 --> 00:39:31,577
<i>Because once I'm done with you,</i>

519
00:39:31,660 --> 00:39:33,746
<i>you'll never be able to smile again.</i>

520
00:39:41,212 --> 00:39:44,965
[tense music playing]

521
00:40:02,316 --> 00:40:03,818
Congratulations.

522
00:40:09,407 --> 00:40:13,327
Red roses for you, Red Dragon.

523
00:40:19,333 --> 00:40:21,043
You think it's going to be that easy?

524
00:40:21,127 --> 00:40:24,213
You think I'll let you
off the hook so easily?

525
00:40:24,296 --> 00:40:26,757
Mark my words. I won't stop.

526
00:40:26,841 --> 00:40:29,635
Even if I have to file
multiple cases against you,

527
00:40:29,718 --> 00:40:34,265
I'll do it just to prove that you,
Helena Montoya, are Red Dragon.

528
00:40:34,348 --> 00:40:37,393
Go ahead. Who's going to believe you?

529
00:40:38,310 --> 00:40:39,228
[chuckles]

530
00:40:39,311 --> 00:40:40,855
You don't have a witness.

531
00:40:42,022 --> 00:40:43,274
The Big Four are dead.

532
00:40:43,691 --> 00:40:45,192
And so is Mercedes.

533
00:40:46,026 --> 00:40:50,030
And your witness just backed out.

534
00:40:50,114 --> 00:40:51,365
[laughs]

535
00:40:51,449 --> 00:40:55,619
Who's going to prove that I am Red Dragon?

536
00:40:58,289 --> 00:40:59,415
I will.

537
00:41:01,834 --> 00:41:03,544
I'll testify against you.

538
00:41:04,378 --> 00:41:05,463
Really?

539
00:41:06,922 --> 00:41:08,048
You?

540
00:41:08,632 --> 00:41:12,928
You'll testify against me, Diego Torillo?

541
00:41:13,804 --> 00:41:15,931
Well, it's your word against mine.

542
00:41:16,765 --> 00:41:20,811
You might be forgetting
that you were my ally once.

543
00:41:21,479 --> 00:41:23,939
And I'll make it appear
you're testifying against me

544
00:41:24,023 --> 00:41:26,567
because the real leader
of this organization

545
00:41:26,650 --> 00:41:28,777
is none other than, Lily.

546
00:41:29,737 --> 00:41:33,240
Then while the citizens
of Ardiente are crucifying you,

547
00:41:33,324 --> 00:41:37,953
I am going to leave this
detention area free as a bird.

548
00:41:38,829 --> 00:41:44,043
Enough time for me to build
a new syndicate group.

549
00:41:45,169 --> 00:41:48,214
What should I call my new syndicate?

550
00:41:48,297 --> 00:41:49,924
Let's see.

551
00:41:50,799 --> 00:41:51,842
Poison Ivy?

552
00:41:52,927 --> 00:41:54,762
Oh! How about…

553
00:41:55,721 --> 00:41:57,431
Tiger Lily?

554
00:41:59,600 --> 00:42:02,228
I'll do that and make it appear

555
00:42:02,311 --> 00:42:05,856
that you're the leader of that syndicate!

556
00:42:05,940 --> 00:42:08,567
-You will, huh?!
-Stop hurting me! Ouch!

557
00:42:08,651 --> 00:42:10,819
Help me! I'm being hurt!

558
00:42:10,903 --> 00:42:12,238
Stop hurting me!

559
00:42:12,321 --> 00:42:14,698
Oh my God! Did you see that?!

560
00:42:14,782 --> 00:42:19,245
She's hurting me! Did you see that?!

561
00:42:19,328 --> 00:42:22,456
People like Lily Cruz are the reason

562
00:42:22,540 --> 00:42:25,209
why I'm involved in this case!

563
00:42:25,960 --> 00:42:27,002
It's her!

564
00:42:27,086 --> 00:42:29,463
Please, officer! Arrest her!

565
00:42:29,547 --> 00:42:32,466
[camera shutter clicking]

566
00:42:37,513 --> 00:42:38,806
Please, arrest her!

567
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:43,394
Officer, arrest her! She was hurting me!

568
00:42:49,692 --> 00:42:51,986
You're such a good actress!

569
00:42:52,069 --> 00:42:54,822
But the real criminal here is you!

570
00:42:56,407 --> 00:43:02,121
Just wait because I'll prove
you're a crime lord.

571
00:43:04,373 --> 00:43:07,042
I am telling you, I'm going to prove it!

572
00:43:07,126 --> 00:43:08,252
Please, arrest her!

573
00:43:08,335 --> 00:43:11,630
-Come with me outside, ma'am.
-Don't touch me!

574
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:20,764
Did you see that?
I was just here, you know.

575
00:43:22,224 --> 00:43:24,018
I didn't even have bodyguards.

576
00:43:24,101 --> 00:43:28,606
I feel so helpless and she just
attacked me with that guy,

577
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:32,192
Diego Torillo. I feel so violated!

578
00:43:32,943 --> 00:43:36,822
After I've been proven innocent,
she's going to do that to me?

579
00:43:36,905 --> 00:43:40,909
Why? Why would she do that?
I can't even think of a reason.

580
00:43:40,993 --> 00:43:42,995
She used to be my friend, you know.

581
00:43:46,332 --> 00:43:47,916
-Lily.
-Lily.

582
00:43:48,834 --> 00:43:50,002
[door slams shut]

583
00:43:50,919 --> 00:43:51,962
Lily!

584
00:43:56,967 --> 00:43:58,719
-[knocking on door]
-Lily!

585
00:43:58,802 --> 00:44:00,596
Lily, open the door!

586
00:44:00,679 --> 00:44:02,014
-[knocking on door]
-Lily!

587
00:44:02,723 --> 00:44:03,641
[Diego] Lily!

588
00:44:04,141 --> 00:44:05,934
-[knocking on door]
-Lily!

589
00:44:06,602 --> 00:44:08,062
[knocking on door]

590
00:44:08,145 --> 00:44:09,229
[Diego] Lily!

591
00:44:12,358 --> 00:44:13,651
-[glass shatters]
-[screams]

592
00:44:14,860 --> 00:44:16,153
-[glass shatters]
-[screams]

593
00:44:19,281 --> 00:44:23,702
All of my efforts, wasted!

594
00:44:23,786 --> 00:44:24,745
[panting]

595
00:44:24,828 --> 00:44:26,830
-Lily!
-Villanueva?

596
00:44:26,914 --> 00:44:29,750
-Yes, ma'am?
-Get the keys from the study room.

597
00:44:29,833 --> 00:44:31,085
-Hurry.
-Yes, ma'am.

598
00:44:31,168 --> 00:44:32,461
Lily!

599
00:44:32,544 --> 00:44:36,757
[dramatic music playing]

600
00:44:36,840 --> 00:44:39,176
Everything I did was for nothing.

601
00:44:51,730 --> 00:44:53,857
[sniffles, sobs]

602
00:45:04,660 --> 00:45:07,621
<i>Now isn't the time to give up.</i>
<i>Keep fighting.</i>

603
00:45:07,704 --> 00:45:09,540
[Lily] <i>I'll take justice</i>
<i>into my own hands.</i>

604
00:45:09,623 --> 00:45:12,292
<i>If it's a fight that they want,</i>
<i>then I'll give it to them.</i>

605
00:45:12,376 --> 00:45:15,421
<i>-What's going on, Papa?</i>
<i>-It's showtime. Viva Ardiente!</i>

606
00:45:15,504 --> 00:45:16,880
[henchman 1] <i>What's your</i>
<i>plan now, Boss Jaguar?</i>

607
00:45:16,964 --> 00:45:20,092
<i>The Ardientes have become more powerful</i>
<i>with Red Dragon on their side.</i>

608
00:45:20,175 --> 00:45:22,803
[henchman 2] <i>Shouldn't we be</i>
<i>joining their group now?</i>

609
00:45:22,886 --> 00:45:25,347
<i>Don't worry. We'll bring them down.</i>

610
00:45:25,431 --> 00:45:27,558
<i>We couldn't get the court</i>
<i>to release a search warrant.</i>

611
00:45:27,641 --> 00:45:29,768
<i>Wasn't the evidence we presented enough?</i>

612
00:45:29,852 --> 00:45:31,103
<i>I am not a vigilante.</i>

613
00:45:31,186 --> 00:45:34,148
<i>It's my job to make sure</i>
<i>the law is enforced.</i>

614
00:45:34,231 --> 00:45:37,359
<i>The law of Lily Cruz will prevail.</i>

615
00:45:37,443 --> 00:45:39,695
[theme music playing]
